## WebClerk3 Sales Order Schema

Based on the available types and API structure, WebClerk3 uses a more consolidated approach:

### SalesOrder (Header)
- `id`: Primary key
- `sales_order_no`: Order number
- `dt_created`: Creation timestamp
- `.metadata`: JSONB for additional fields (likely consolidates profile1-6, custom fields)
- `.prefs`: JSONB for user preferences
- `.refs`: JSONB for relationships (customer, contacts, etc.)

### SalesOrderLine (Detail)
- `id`: Primary key
- `parent`: Foreign key to sales_order
- `item_id`: Item reference
- `item_name`: Item name
- `description`: Item description
- `quantity`: Order quantity
- `price`: Object with `sell` and `cost` prices
- `discount_amount`: Discount
- `extended_price`: Calculated extended price
- `unit_cost`: Unit cost
- `line_margin`: Calculated margin
- `dt_created/modified`: Timestamps

